# Template for .env, the local-only file for this repo's secrets.
# Copy it (cp .env.example .env) and fill in the values. .env is ignored by git.

# NPM_TOKEN
# An npm granular access token that can publish @paperclerk/n8n-nodes-paperclerk.
#
# Make it on npmjs.com, signed in as the npm account paperclerk (the @paperclerk
# scope is that account's): Access Tokens > Generate New Token > Granular Access Token.
#   Expiration:          up to 90 days (npm's limit for tokens that can publish)
#   Bypass 2FA:          on (GitHub Actions cannot answer a 2FA prompt)
#   Packages and scopes: Read and write, on the @paperclerk scope
#
# The GitHub Action that publishes reads it from the repository secret
# NPM_TOKEN, not from this file. Load that secret from .env with the
# PaperClerk GitHub account active (gh auth switch --user PaperClerk):
#
#   grep '^NPM_TOKEN=' .env | cut -d= -f2- | gh secret set NPM_TOKEN --repo UsePaperclerk/n8n-nodes-paperclerk
#
# Once the package is on npm, trusted publishing (npmjs.com > the package >
# Settings > Trusted publishing: GitHub Actions, UsePaperclerk,
# n8n-nodes-paperclerk, publish.yml) replaces the token: then delete the
# repository secret and revoke the token.
NPM_TOKEN=
